; walk-cxx-sbx — a pattern loop in progress beats a break on its row.
;
; `SB0` marks row 0; `SB1` on row 2 runs the loop once; `C02` sits on the
; same row and loses the first time round, then is honoured the second,
; when there is no loop left to make.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
